<title>USA: First Chicago NBD Corp Q3 net higher.</title>
<headline>First Chicago NBD Corp Q3 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary	     $ 1.09		  $  1.07</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 1.08		     1.06</p>
<p> Net			358,000		  357,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     320,200		  324,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     327,500		  331,800</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 net includes charge of $18 million or $0.04 a share from recapitalization of the Savings Association Insurance Fund.  </p>
<p>	  NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary	     $ 3.24		 $   3.07</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 3.19		     3.03</p>
<p> Net		    1,059,000		1,024,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     319,800		  323,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     327,200		  331,200</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 nine months net includes charge of $18 million or $0.04 a share from recapitalization of the Savings Association Insurance Fund.  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 combined trading losses totaled $12 million vs profits of $85 million in the 1995 third quarter.</p>
<p>Assets $106.69 billion vs $124.06 billion</p>
<p>Loans $66.60 billion vs $61.08 billion</p>
<p>Deposits $63.68 billion vs $66.93 billion</p>
<p>	     Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
